/Users/lchingen/hivemind-step2-identity-2026-11-09/clean-arch/step2-identity-2026-11-09/INVESTIGATION.md:77:Two independent AI readers received the same 12 anonymized record pairs and both complete stored articles, with no prior Jev answers, selection reasons or case key. Full unedited opinions: `blind-codex.md` (SHA-256 d2a87985e7645caf4f22b5488c0e4e1d215e2bbe4771f9876b5407888d672b7b), `blind-claude.md` (b7b71c1f30b69cf8a62b542abb012b8d65522b4b85944d4865ff89fb639f44c1). They agree on 8/12: B01, B02, B06 same; B03, B05, B10, B12 different; B09 supersedes, with both pointing out the denial is already in the earlier article and its timing is unclear. They disagree on B04 (same vs uncertain), B07 (same vs different), B08 (supersedes vs different), B11 (same vs uncertain). An independently blinded third reader (`blind-third.md`) gives B04 uncertain, B07 different, B08 different, B11 same, explaining unresolved source and record-boundary issues. Majority vote is not gold and the original disagreement is retained. In particular B11's two sources describe potentially different payment mechanics, so calling the same announcement the same record requires judgment about which detail matters; B04's base and underlying analyst set cannot be established from the source. B08's leak is not overturned by a later launch even though its unconfirmed-status caveat changes. These are AI source readings on selected cases, not population accuracy.
/Users/lchingen/hivemind-step2-identity-2026-11-09/clean-arch/step2-identity-2026-11-09/INVESTIGATION.md:87:The description above of the 70% incoming record is shorthand for source context, not the actual model input: the source text and the record's numerical `basis` carry the supply-constraint context, but the exact incoming comparison `piece_text` contains its summary and passages, neither of which includes that phrase. The old 9:e5 comparison text does include the supply-constraint statement. Thus the model sees incomplete context, but that alone does not prove this missing context caused its wrong relation. The chosen format deliberately excludes `figures` under clean PRD §14, so showing them is a proposed contract change, not a routine bug fix. The completed source-backed readings independently call the Hugging Face 30→20 pair the same announced deal, not an update. Claude also traced an earlier false split 20→8 and 14→9, which must be checked as a cascade rather than three independent failures (`claude-r1.md`). D392 Stage 2 has since finished (main commit 9552c8d); the formerly live-run status in older notes is historical, not current.
reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/codex-reflection.md:5:Provisional position: continue Jev as the current comparison baseline, without presenting it as validated or fixed. The comparator experiment is deliberately selected and reveals one clear B05 regression versus fresh Jev single and one clear H01 improvement; neither model nor an ensemble is proven overall better. Provider, format and candidate batch differ, and pair labels do not select a group. R05 is contested. A three-draw single 6-case comparison cannot establish overall precision/recall. Jev remains a three-way judge over search results; retrieval recall, the validity of revisions, single-to-batch sensitivity, false group splits and correct persistence all matter. Actual Jev output `supersedes` does not itself make text disappear; source records remain stored, though relationships could mislead downstream readers. Baseline numerical lines: D381 fresh search 141/145 full-system available reference pairs, 1 clear wrong merge /57 plus 2 overlaps, detail retention 22=22; one draw, narrow reference, clustered 55 pairs and almost no revisions. None is overall precision or recall.
reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/codex-challenge-response.md:3:举个例子：Jev 三次都没认出 H01 的同一笔收购公告，DeepSeek 三次都认出来；但在 B05，DeepSeek 三次都把两种不同的增长说法连成修订，Jev 单独比较三次没有犯这个错误，完整请求却犯了两次。**这说明两边各有问题，不能得出谁整体更好。**
reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/codex-challenge-response.md:31:这能检验 B05 和 P01 暴露的风险有多广，以及错误来自判断、写入还是展示。**它不能判断 DeepSeek 或生成式分析整体是否更好**；56 也不是独立案例数或最终错误数。它是目前最便宜、能先检验是否应继续依赖现有 Jev 路径的行动。[待查范围](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-step2-identity-2026-11-09/clean-arch/step2-identity-2026-11-09/results-claude.md:84)。
reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/codex-challenge.md:1:Challenge your own conclusion and my independent reflection (`codex-reflection.md`) before we tell Alex “Jev is the way.” Specifically: (1) fresh c8 1/57 is a wrong-merge line, not overall precision and ignores misses and false revision edges; previous 3/104 failed under other Step1 inputs, do not compare as controlled versions; (2) H01 is Jev-stable failure, DeepSeek 3/3 correct; B05 DeepSeek worse than Jev single, but full Jev also erred 2/3, so the same-pair experiment does not establish Jev beats DeepSeek on product or overall. Does “best supported” mean lowest integration burden rather than proven quality? (3) the historic 2026-10-27 D201 results show Jev 7/18 vs a generative analysis call handling 20/21 and 3/3 under a different old contract, inputs and lots of context; should we disclose it as not equivalent rather than ignore contrary evidence? (4) R05 is disputed and P01 full produces a second unadjudicated edge; do not report improvements or controls as unambiguous. (5) score-threshold 363 count is not independent; ± no numerical superiority claim. What single recommendation answers whether keep Jev, which would change your mind, and what is the cheapest source-backed next action? Cite exact evidence. Read-only no writes or paid calls, out of scope everything except Step2.
