reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/claude-independent.md:60:- **漏并**：同一句话变成两条看似独立的记录，之后的重复只进其中一组。B05 的请求里，70% 指引就同时躺在 14:e2 和 9:e1 两组。
reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/claude-independent.md:67:- **所以要分两种错。** H01、R05 是稳定的、有把握的错，重发不会好。B05、B10 和对照 B01 是差 0.15 以内的擦边判断，写进库的结果每次运行可能不同。
reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/claude-independent.md:68:- **DeepSeek 的 3/3 也不等于把握。** 它没有分数。B05 三次推理长度差很多（620–1595 个推理 token），标签都一样，说明它的错也稳定。
reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/claude-independent.md:70:- **排序。** B05 完整请求里三条候选都被判"同一句"：14:e2 是 0.89–0.90，另两条 0.60–0.70。第一名三次都稳（差距至少 0.19）。第二、三名互换或打平，其中一条（分析师预期）本身就不该算同一句，是排序把它挡掉的。头两名差距小于约 0.1 时，进哪一组会随运行变。这种情况在已存数据里有多少，没人数过。
reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/claude-independent.md:78:- 唯一测过的替代品没有分数，在产品形式下只在 H01 上无争议地更好。
reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/claude-independent.md:98:- **材料都在。** `poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/settled.json` 的 `repeat_groups` 有 26 组，55 个"重复"成员加 1 个"修订"成员，运行前冻结。搜索那条线用过同一份对应关系（`step2/search-misses.json`）。结果在 `step2/library.json` 和 `decisions.json`。
reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/claude-challenge.md:1:Challenge your independent conclusion with the read-only Codex review and its response: read `reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/codex-independent.md` and `codex-challenge-response.md`, plus our own `codex-reflection.md`. In particular: (1) withdraw any appearance that Jev is proven best: integration/validation history is not accuracy, user asks keep now vs best long term; 85% subjective confidence has no calibrated evidence, remove it. (2) B05 Jev full 1/3 different, single 3/3 different; this is an observed difference between presentation modes, although 3 draws, 0.02–0.05 scores and same-mode variance cannot establish true batching effect; do not assert no sensitivity or treat scores as calibrated coin flips. (3) six requests for H01 are 3 full and 3 single, not 6 statistically independent same-form draws. (4) `gold-v1` v2 post-send correction means historical 20/21 vs 7/18 is not valid and input/contract differ; codex found old clean action 10/21 and 2/3 instead. What does that counterevidence really prove? (5) B10 frozen source-matter reference says revision, blind statements say different; clearly preserve conflict and do not silently redefine frozen reference. (6) R05 fresh blinded reader explicitly finds a real publisher update plausible; it is unresolved, and P01 extra edge also disputed. (7) Which next no-cost work is most useful: all 56 historical revision answers source-backed, or frozen 55 repeat-member outcomes? Could 55 reference coverage rely on mapped nonmatching/bundled units? Confirm with actual files and recommend one test with valid denominators and explicit falsifier. Cite evidence, distinguish product judgment and storage. Converge or preserve differences; no edits, paid calls, live DB or unrelated work.
reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/codex-second-challenge.md:1:Your Claude colleague's independent report proposes a different first no-cost test: in fresh pre-run settled.json, 26 groups have 55 later members labeled repeat and one labeled revision, 145 prior/later pairs; reconcile those 55 members through extraction, retrieval, Jev answer and actual group placement to quantify missed repeats, then personally source-read every miss. You proposed reviewing 56 Jev-supersedes answers. User asks whether Jev is still the best direction, and H01 directly shows a retrieval-success/comparison failure. Which one most efficiently answers that question first, and what blind spots remain? Check the actual settled.json structure and source-matter vs bundled-record identity caveat; old same-quote mapping was proven wrong for Sharon/Firmus. Do not change frozen labels or equate missing extraction to Jev miss, or infer independence from repeated stories. Also explicitly correct B05 statement that 3+3 draws prove request form causes it: they show observed difference but sample and stochastic provider limits preclude causal attribution. Recommend only one source-backed no-cost test with a concrete counterexample/falsifier, preserve dissent if real. Read-only, no API calls, no writes, no live DB.
reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/codex-second.stderr:13:Your Claude colleague's independent report proposes a different first no-cost test: in fresh pre-run settled.json, 26 groups have 55 later members labeled repeat and one labeled revision, 145 prior/later pairs; reconcile those 55 members through extraction, retrieval, Jev answer and actual group placement to quantify missed repeats, then personally source-read every miss. You proposed reviewing 56 Jev-supersedes answers. User asks whether Jev is still the best direction, and H01 directly shows a retrieval-success/comparison failure. Which one most efficiently answers that question first, and what blind spots remain? Check the actual settled.json structure and source-matter vs bundled-record identity caveat; old same-quote mapping was proven wrong for Sharon/Firmus. Do not change frozen labels or equate missing extraction to Jev miss, or infer independence from repeated stories. Also explicitly correct B05 statement that 3+3 draws prove request form causes it: they show observed difference but sample and stochastic provider limits preclude causal attribution. Recommend only one source-backed no-cost test with a concrete counterexample/falsifier, preserve dissent if real. Read-only, no API calls, no writes, no live DB.
