 frozen gold. No edits, no API sends, no paid experiments.
reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/codex-challenge.stderr:102:Provisional position: continue Jev as the current comparison baseline, without presenting it as validated or fixed. The comparator experiment is deliberately selected and reveals one clear B05 regression versus fresh Jev single and one clear H01 improvement; neither model nor an ensemble is proven overall better. Provider, format and candidate batch differ, and pair labels do not select a group. R05 is contested. A three-draw single 6-case comparison cannot establish overall precision/recall. Jev remains a three-way judge over search results; retrieval recall, the validity of revisions, single-to-batch sensitivity, false group splits and correct persistence all matter. Actual Jev output `supersedes` does not itself make text disappear; source records remain stored, though relationships could mislead downstream readers. Baseline numerical lines: D381 fresh search 141/145 full-system available reference pairs, 1 clear wrong merge /57 plus 2 overlaps, detail retention 22=22; one draw, narrow reference, clustered 55 pairs and almost no revisions. None is overall precision or recall.
