reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/codex-independent.jsonl:38:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'H01|B05|B10|R05|P01|56|miss|revision|material|ranking' COUNCIL-LOOP.md INVESTIGATION.md results-codex.md results-claude.md result-blind-codex.md result-blind-claude.md r05-adjudication.md results-codex-followup.md\"","aggregated_output":"(eval):5: parse error near `end'\n(eval):5: parse error near `end'\nresults-codex-followup.md:1:**P01 对 `45:e3` 的修订链接应标为“有争议”，不能算已验证正确。** 因此，P01 的目标关系答对了，不能说明这条记录写出的所有关系都正确。\nresults-codex-followup.md:5:实际 Jev 请求中的新记录只概括为 Nvidia 拒绝“延期说法”，没有带上新文章提到备用方案的上下文。按现行规则，只有回应了旧记录的**主陈述**才算修订；是否可以把这句宽泛回应扩展到 `45:e3`，现有材料不足以确定。见 [完整来源 P01](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-step2-identity-2026-11-09/clean-arch/step2-identity-2026-11-09/blind-positive-revisions.json)、[完整 Jev 请求，P01 q2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-step2-identity-2026-11-09/clean-arch/step2-identity-2026-11-09/probe-2026-11-09/bodies.json) 和 [比较规则](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-step2-identity-2026-11-09/clean-arch/step2/compare.py:57)。\nresults-codex-followup.md:9:**R05 我也要收窄之前的结论。** 我仍倾向于“不属于修订”：Nvidia 解释了缺货，但没有确认或否认停产。新的盲读指出，同一家媒体后来采用了更谨慎的表述，且零售商更改了商品状态；这使“后续报道是否改变了原推测”存在合理边界争议。因此，独立比较器的 `different` 是**有来源支持的改善线索**，不应再称为无争议地纠正了错误链接。见 [结果盲读 T06](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-step2-identity-2026-11-09/clean-arch/step2-identity-2026-11-09/result-blind-codex.md)。\nresults-codex.md:1:**结论：独立比较器这条线应停止，不应围着 B05 调提示词。** 它在两个例子上答得更好，却在 B05 连续三次把两种不同的增长说法连成“修订”。不过，[RESULTS-DRAFT.md](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-step2-identity-2026-11-09/clean-arch/step2-identity-2026-11-09/RESULTS-DRAFT.md) 把它说成“触发预先写好的自动停止条件”，这句话需要改：最终规则只把 **B01 和 P01** 明确列为回退停止对照，B05 不在其中。B05 是严重的新回退，是停止这条方案的充分研究判断；不能事后改写成原先明确规定的触发条件。见 [最终结果规则](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-step2-identity-2026-11-09/clean-arch/step2-identity-2026-11-09/HARNESS-DESIGN.md:100)。\nresults-codex.md:3:**B05 的回退有原文依据。** 新记录是公司对 FY2028 收入增长 **70% 的正式预测**；旧记录是 Kress 说客户预测显示收入**可能翻倍**，并附 Huang 说不受供应限制时增长可能更高。旧文章同时写了 70% 和客户预测，支持它们是并列的不同说法，而不是一条修订另一条。\nresults-codex.md:5:比较器看到的文字也已经区分“公司预测”和“客户预测”，但有缺口：新记录的摘要和引文没有写 70% 受供应限制；旧记录的原始陈述日期未知。两篇报道对 70% 的个人说话人归属也不完全一致。**所以可以判断这条修订关系缺乏支持，但不能断言模型为什么犯错，或断言补上供应限制就一定能修好。** 原文见 [B05 来源](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-step2-identity-2026-11-09/clean-arch/step2-identity-2026-11-09/source-blind-packet.json)；实际两边文字见 [本次请求](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-step2-identity-2026-11-09/clean-arch/step2-identity-2026-11-09/probe-2026-11-09/bodies.json)。\nresults-codex.md:11:| B05：两种增长说法应不同 | 1/3 判不同 | 3/3 判不同 | **0/3 判不同** | 相同对子文字下，新比较器比 Jev 单独比较退步；完整候选请求本身也有 2/3 错误。 |\nresults-codex.md:12:| B10：交付与收入占比应不同 | **2/3 判不同** | 1/3 判不同 | 3/3 判不同 | 新比较器对子判断更稳定；不能说它已证明分组优于完整产品路径。完整 Jev 有两次也没有把它并入错误组。 |\nresults-codex.md:13:| H01：同一收购公告 | 0/3 判重复 | 0/3 判重复 | 3/3 判重复 | 新比较器在这个漏合并例子上有改善线索。 |\nresults-codex.md:14:| R05：公司未确认停产 | 0/3 判不同 | 0/3 判不同 | 3/3 判不同 | 新比较器在这个错误修订例子上有改善线索；旧记录的原始说话人字段有已知归属问题。 |\nresults-codex.md:15:| B01、P01 | 两个对照均 3/3 符合预期 | 同左 | 同左 | B01 是重复报道对照。P01 只支持识别官方否认；不能代表后来修改预测等所有修订。 |\nresults-codex.md:17:B10 的完整请求中，第 1 次只有目标组被判重复；后两次没有任何候选被判重复，因此按现有代码分别是**错误并组一次、新建组两次**。独立比较器只对一个对子给标签，没有组排名或其他候选答案，不能直接写成“三次都把产品分到正确组”。见 [事件记录](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-step2-identity-2026-11-09/clean-arch/step2-identity-2026-11-09/probe-2026-11-09/events.jsonl) 和 [分组代码](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-step2-identity-2026-11-09/clean-arch/step2/compare.py:109)。\nresults-codex.md:19:**完整请求和单独请求不能混为一个对照。** B05 两者结果不同，说明本次样本对请求形式敏感；它还不能证明是其他候选造成的，更不能把新比较器的差异全部归因于模型。提供商、请求格式和输出方式也不同。重复发送相同内容是三次请求，但不能保证提供商内部采样彼此独立。\nresults-codex.md:25:**下一步建议只做一个零费用研究：**逐条检查这次完整请求里，哪些其他候选与目标说法相似、模型同时给了什么关系，以及这些关系写入后会怎样展示；用保存的实际输入和答案重放，不改提示词、不发送请求。决定性结果是：如果 B05 的错误关系在单独与完整请求之间变化，但其他类似案例没有一致可解释的候选干扰，就不能把“联合上下文”当作已找到的通用原因；反过来也只得到值得后续验证的机制线索，不能据此恢复已停止的比较器方案。\nresults-claude.md:5:- **但结果稿里的停止理由写错了。** 按冻结规则（`HARNESS-DESIGN.md:100`），\"可重复退步\"只针对 B01 和 P01 两个对照。B05 不在这个定义里。照字面读，规则给出的是\"在 H01、R05、B10 上有选定案例改善，B05 是一个稳定的错答\"，而不是\"B05 触发停止\"。\nresults-claude.md:6:- **停下这条线我同意维持。** 一是你要求维持；二是对着产品真实走的完整批量对照，这个比较器只在 H01、R05 上明确更好。但要改的是记录下来的理由，不能拿\"看完结果再挑规则\"来重开这条线或采纳比较器。\nresults-claude.md:13:  - B05：8a47253e…（`case-key.json:56`）\nresults-claude.md:14:  - B10：70056b2c…（`:116`）\nresults-claude.md:16:  - B05 三个臂里，新记录和已存记录的文字逐字相同（`bodies.json:20-22`）。\nresults-claude.md:21:## 2. B05：原文、两段原话，以及它算不算触发停止\nresults-claude.md:37:**为什么 B05 在记录层面是模糊的**\nresults-claude.md:45:- 按规则的字面，B05 不触发停止。\nresults-claude.md:46:- 但 B05 说明比较器并不是处处更好：在一个模糊的对子上，它 3 次都很确定地重犯了产品原来的错。\nresults-claude.md:48:- 不应该围着 B05 去调提示词。\nresults-claude.md:50:## 3. B10：对完整批量产品对照，并没有明确改善\nresults-claude.md:57:- **结果稿里的\"B10 改善\"只是相对 Jev 单问**（单问 3 次里只对 1 次，而且都是 0.45 对 0.44 这种接近打平的回答）。\nresults-claude.md:64:  - **对单问基准：** H01、R05、B10 有改善，B05 变差。\nresults-claude.md:65:  - **对完整批量（产品）基准：** 只有 H01、R05 明确改善（3/3 对 0/3），B10 只多对 1 次，B05 多错 1 次。\nresults-claude.md:69:- **H01：** Jev 稳定地判不同，0.59–0.60 对 0.37–0.38（`events.jsonl:25, 60, 80`），会多出一个重复组。DeepSeek 能避免。\nresults-claude.md:70:- **R05：** Jev 稳定地判 supersedes，约 0.86–0.88，会多一行误导读者的 \"Revises\"。DeepSeek 能避免。\nresults-claude.md:71:- **B05：** 如果用 DeepSeek，这行错误的 \"Revises\" 会 3 次都出现。\nresults-claude.md:72:- **B01、P01：** 三个臂都一致。\nresults-claude.md:75:- **B05 算不算\"可重复退步\"：** 结果稿（`RESULTS-DRAFT.md:14`）和冻结规则（`HARNESS-DESIGN.md:100`）的说法冲突。更早的 council 证伪条件（`codex-challenge-v2.md:72`）会把 B05 列为决定性案例。三份依据并不一致。\nresults-claude.md:76:- **B05 的参照：** \"不同\"这个判断有原文支持（新旧两轮盲读者都这么判），但它部分依赖只有原文里才有的信息。只看记录文字，supersedes 也有一条字面上说得通的路径。说话人归属也不清楚。\nresults-claude.md:77:- **B10：** 两位读者都判 different。但 13:e4 本身有归属问题（`COUNCIL-LOOP.md:24`）。\nresults-claude.md:78:- **P01：** 只能作为\"官方否认已报道说法\"的有界对照。否认早已出现在旧文章里，时间先后不清楚，不能用来声称一般性的修订能力。\nresults-claude.md:79:- **R05：** 已存记录的 `original_party` 写成 Nvidia，但它的层级是 rumour。DeepSeek 没被这个字段误导。\nresults-claude.md:80:- **独立的盲读复核还在进行中**（`RESULTS-DRAFT.md:18`）。DeepSeek 的推理过程按设计全部丢弃了（`HARNESS-DESIGN.md:108`），所以无法从存档里拿到它对 B05 的自述。\nresults-claude.md:84:- 选 D392 d1：56 个 supersedes 回答，涉及 34 条记录。\nresults-claude.md:94:3. **两位读者都不支持的边里，关键信息是否本来就在比较文本里？** 例如 R05 的 \"neither confirm nor deny\"。\nresult-blind-codex.md:9:**T02 — `different`.** The stored record’s main statement is that Kress said **customer forecasts** indicated revenue “may double next year.” The incoming record’s main statement is the company’s **70% fiscal 2028 revenue growth forecast**. The stored article itself separately reports both: the 70% guidance and the customer-demand indication. The incoming article also says unconstrained growth could be “a lot higher” than 70%, but that overlap with the stored record’s secondary Huang statement does not make the main statements identical. The incoming $673 billion–$700 billion figure is the article’s calculation from consensus, not a separately attributed Nvidia forecast. The articles were published September 5 and 6; that order does not establish a revision of customer demand.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:5:- Objective: diagnose and find a general, measurable improvement for wrong grouping, missed grouping and incorrect update relations on the clean Step 2 path, without changing frozen ruler files or the adopted configuration.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:6:- Reference: c8 Step 1 plus current clean Step 2 Jev 1.14.0, the original saved requests and forward decisions. D381's chosen acceptance lines: at least 90% search, at most 2% clear wrong merges, no loss of later details in grouped dossiers. These do not by themselves cover missed grouping, incorrect revision edges, downstream utility, or an independent comparator's quality; no new pass line has been approved.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:7:- The ruler remains AGENTS §7.1 golden-v5: dev SHA 6f9476bb… and test af2145cd… (`golden-v5.sha256`); for the historical clean Step 2 run its frozen source-backed reference and D381 line are retained with their stated scope. New AI source readers are diagnostic opinions, not replacements for the frozen ruler. Pairwise selected examples are not a benchmark.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:8:- Scope: Step 2 comparison, candidate context and its actual grouping/revision consequences; unrelated Step 1 changes, downstream redesign, production migration, broader acceptance and frozen-file edits are outside scope. Users' eventual decision is required for a changed product behavior. A paid run beyond a few-cent probe or a full forward acceptance requires Alex's explicit word (AGENTS §9); budget for any proposed probe must be fixed from actual bytes before sending. No new paid diagnostic has been sent.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:12:See `INVESTIGATION.md`, `stored-census.md` in the prior report and `claude-r1.md`. Stored outcomes: fresh 1 clear wrong/57 merge decisions plus two overlaps; three dev draws 1 wrong instance each, including a repeated pair, so not independent samples. 84 revision edges over the four stored runs, not a measured error rate. A false revision on 19→9:e5 remains independent of earlier separate groups for the 70% guidance; 30→20 is a wrong revision on an already duplicated announcement. Earlier 20→8 was a missed repeat according to direct source reading. Deliberately chosen blind source cases have disagreement; no performance inference.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:24:Direct check: completed `reader-packet.json` source `gnews:26fd862b0d58999b7451b493` (2026-09-05) describes Nvidia's Thursday $12.9bn announcement; source `gnews:243636e860a787a59c4d0c7a` (2026-09-06) describes its Thursday $13bn announcement, same company and target. This supports the 20→8 missed repeat as a source-backed lead. Neither article independently proves the truth of the acquisition. Fresh record `13:e4` attributes the production statement to Nvidia while the stored quotation states it in the reporter's voice; this limits source-attribution confidence, separately from the clear distinction between the revenue-share forecast and August deliveries. No Step 1 change follows in this scope.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:26:The previously frozen 12-pair pilot covers the later 30→20 false revision but not the antecedent 20→8 false split. It must not be sent or reported as testing missed repeats; fixing the candidate list changes the frozen diagnostic manifest and requires a new hash and independent source-backed controls before any send. Earlier planned same-input comparator also does not fix retrieval misses or define disagreement handling; its source observations cannot estimate full-forward performance.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:31:`claude-challenge-v2.md` independently agrees that the prior 12-pair packet omits 20→8 and 14→9, that comparison input excludes figures intentionally, and that revision links need their own review. It retracts its earlier confident B08 revision label after seeing the record's main statement and reader disagreement. Two independent source readers consider B05 different and B06 the same statement. Its suggested 20-pair, five-arm, three-draw plan is a 300-call, roughly $0.65 estimated probe; this exceeds the project's few-cent probe allowance and is not authorized by a request for a council review. Its claims that a second model failing proves an input limitation, that a missed merge alone causes a later false revision, or that an added article publication date establishes statement chronology are not established. Its source-backed useful detail is that the 70% basis is an unverified model-written paraphrase outside the attached passages; the actual comparison already distinguishes management guidance and customer forecasts. Its B08 conclusion remains a source interpretation, not a gold correction. Both reviewers are being challenged on these points, scope and a smaller test (`claude-challenge-v3.txt`, `codex-challenge-v3.txt`).\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:35:Two new source-blind readers (`blind-missed-codex.md`, `blind-missed-claude.md`) independently judge both H01 (20→8, announcement $12.9bn vs $13bn) and H02 (14→9, 70% outlook) to be the same main statement, while documenting uncertainty in reported individual speaker attribution and rounding. These are independent AI opinions, not frozen gold or evidence that the underlying announcement happened.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:37:For potential revision controls, a fixed seed 2401 selected six from the 56 Step 2 `supersedes` answers in the completed D392 clean d1 draw; the list is frozen in `blind-revisions-key.json`. Both source articles were taken from that draw's saved Step 1 requests, with identity checks. `blind-revisions.json` sha256 bed863cc577bc7b4a80a98d25ec45d7fb57b593f9eec850001158b26486bbdd4. Reviewers see no Jev outputs or selection reason. The selection is conditional on Jev's supersedes answers and is not an estimate of overall Step 2 accuracy; this tiny sample is to find source-backed controls and preserve disputes.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:39:After direct challenge, Claude withdrew the claim that two models failing proves the source text is insufficient, withdrew the date-only and unreviewed-figures arms from the first probe, and acknowledged the spending authorization limit. It agreed that preventing an earlier false split does not by itself establish why the later model chose an incorrect revision. It now recommends a same-input Jev full-batch, Jev single-question, independent-model single-question diagnostic, with proper controls and separate interpretation of disputed evidence (`claude-challenge-v3.md`). Both Claude and Codex agree B09 alone is an imperfect positive revision control because the original report already contains the denial; do not present it as satisfying the regression-control gap. The new H01/H02 blind reviews completed after Claude's reply and both independently judged same; the source-backed six-revision audit is still underway. No sender is implemented, no probe is authorized merely by council agreement, and no new model probe has been sent.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:41:## Source-backed revision sample: council B input\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:43:Two independent blind readers received all six fixed-sample pairs. They agree R05 is different (Nvidia explained Shield TV stock shortages without confirming or denying a discontinuation report), R06 is the same statement (two reports of the LangChain release), and R02 is uncertain (a broad platform statement does not clearly address a specific rack delay). They disagreed on R01 (same vs supersedes), R03 (different vs uncertain) and R04 (different vs supersedes). An independent third blinded reader read only the three disputes (`blind-revisions-third.md`): R01 uncertain, R03 different, R04 different. These are AI source opinions, not frozen gold; majority does not remove the recorded disputes. The two unanimous non-revision opinions are leads that the Jev-emitted revision edges were incorrect, subject to source/contract review. The six were randomly drawn conditional on a Jev supersedes choice; several concern the same Kyber story, and a sample of six cannot estimate error rate. The old and new full articles and records are in `blind-revisions.json`; its fixed mapping is in `blind-revisions-key.json`. No clear two-reader valid revision control has been established by this sample; B09 retains the caveat that the denial was already included in the earlier article. No experiment can claim to protect valid revisions until a source-backed control is available.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:45:Codex's source-and-contract challenge (`codex-results-challenge.md`) found R05 a strong wrong-link example, but argues R06 is not equally decisive: an announcement by a related company might also be read as official confirmation, so preserve the ambiguity despite two blind same-statement opinions. It recommends locating a valid revision control before any repair claim and warns that the observed 1/57 wrong-merge rate and targeted missed-repeat cases cannot be compared as population rates. Additional selected possible controls P01/P02 were source-blinded in `blind-positive-revisions.json` (sha256 4fa4fd14003978eea185466ce20b22a78435cc1ed70d2a2640b02945d665f616); these were manually selected as possible controls, not random. One reader finds P01 an official denial of the stored main claim and P02 uncertain; a second blinded reader is in progress. The 20→8 and 14→9 original Jev requests and original answers were independently reconstructed against the completed archive, `missed-pair-requests.json` sha256 09ce47d0220ee29931e053dde957814243c166b231317ca96cf1903f98d20a50. The two candidate control Jev requests also matched the completed D392 archive, `positive-pair-requests.json` sha256 44b0a154fe8ac9e1aa37872fbf9fec5a301189250c577f9ec6b8f95c7ea79f77. This reconstruction does not constitute a source adjudication or send readiness.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:47:P01 (54:e3→45:e1) is now source-blinded by two independent readers: both judge official denial of the Kyber NVL144 delay as `supersedes` (`blind-positive-revisions-codex.md`, `blind-positive-revisions-claude.md`). Both note the original source article already includes the denial, the original response time is unknown, and the old record bundles a separate NVL576 claim not explicitly addressed by the denial. This is a usable but bounded stress control under the current definitions, not an uncontested example of a chronologically later revision or proof that all accompanying statements were denied. P02 remains uncertain/different and is not a positive control. Neither model opinion edits the frozen reference.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:49:Independent follow-up `codex-positive-review.md` accepts P01 as a bounded control for the current report–official-denial relationship. Its caveats do not prohibit a selected-case diagnostic; they do prohibit claiming protection of later forecast revisions without a separate source-backed chronological control. It does not settle NVL576. No reviewer adjudication is treated as frozen gold.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:51:A provisional six-pair shortlist is generated offline in `shortlist-requests-DRAFT.json` (sha256 6b04ccf0919bef6b5aeac6a480dfdcfa7d51b3dc05c1375a0ac2a2965a934654) by `prepare-shortlist.py`. It comprises B01 (valid repeat), B05 (wrong revision), B10 (wrong merge), H01/H02 (missed repeats, H02 has speaker attribution caveat), and P01 (bounded official-denial control). It is not frozen or ready to send: an independent request review is running, a sender and failure controls do not exist, P01 cannot alone establish later-forecast revision protection, and historical Jev answers are not same-day controls. At the repository's dated rates and conservative input/output reservation formula, one draw's 18 calls reserve about $0.0594, and three draws about $0.1782; these estimates are not guaranteed bills. AGENTS §9 requires Alex's explicit word before paid sends beyond a few cents, and a full forward acceptance also has its own authorization boundary. No paid Step 2 call has been sent in this round.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:55:R05's Jev answer is `supersedes` 0.90, even though the incoming summary says Nvidia would neither confirm nor deny discontinuation; this is not a low-score-only failure. The historical Jev requests and answers for R05 and disputed R06 were reconstructed byte for byte from the completed D392 archive in `revision-extra-requests.json` (sha256 e0e75db060dafaede976330311f4fe05937c50d3186b0a9254bb35b2ddbfe2a8). The six-pair shortlist predates R05 and should not be frozen as complete; any new shortlist including it must be regenerated, costed and independently audited. Original-party attribution in the stored R05 record is also suspect; the comparator sees that field, so avoid claiming to know which signal caused Jev's answer.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:57:Council B discussion retains a real sequencing disagreement: Claude proposes first characterizing Jev full-batch vs single-pair repeatability, whereas Codex proposes including the independent comparator in the first paired diagnostic. Either approach needs fresh controls and a bounded source-backed revision control. A passing rerun does not erase the previously observed defect, and a non-reproduced selected case does not establish that a whole class is random noise. Both reviewers were sent a targeted final challenge; no verdict is inferred before they answer.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:61:`codex-final-challenge.md` and `claude-final-challenge.md` converge on a paired diagnostic: fresh Jev full batch, fresh Jev single pair, and an independent same-input comparison in the same round. Claude withdrew its proposed Jev-only stop gate: a later passing draw does not undo an already observed bad write, and a few changing outcomes cannot establish class-wide noise. Both retain R06 as disputed because `same_statement` and official confirmation can overlap; it is excluded from a decisive tally. Both accept P01 only as a bounded direct-denial control, not a later-forecast-change control. Group ranking, disagreement handling and actual forward effects remain untested. Repeated sends are needed to claim repeatability; a single draw can find an obvious failure but cannot establish superiority.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:63:After R05 was reviewed, the offline shortlist was rebuilt to include it alongside B01, B05, B10, H01 and P01. Current `shortlist-requests-DRAFT.json` SHA-256 cb142acfe3491dcf6ccfaa70545ffe3c011e3646a2348b36954b04ec2f3321ce. Dated-price reservations are $0.060671 for one draw of 18 calls and $0.182013 for three draws of 54 calls, excluding uncertain billing, retries and differing provider rates. This supersedes the earlier six-case draft, which contained H02 instead of R05. The updated shortlist is undergoing independent request audit; it is not a frozen manifest, complete sender, approval or a result. Historical source and response files remain immutable. The q12 c13 process previously observed no longer appeared in a later process check, but run status must be rechecked before any new sends. The next actual work is finish no-cost input/control/sender and independent reviews; preserve user authority for sends beyond the few-cent boundary and for any change to production behavior.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:65:`shortlist-audit-r2.md` independently verified the revised six historical archive bodies and original answers, all 18 prepared provider bodies and hashes, unique-case precondition, choice order and reservation calculation. It confirms source packets and blind-reader judgments are not pinned, the response validator and sender are unbuilt, and the set cannot measure overall error rates, retrieval or group ranking. Review of offline request construction does not clear a paid send or constitute an experimental result.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:71:The council recommends rejecting this candidate because of a serious new regression: on B05 the independent model called `supersedes` 3/3 while Jev single called `different` 3/3 (fresh Jev full called `supersedes` 2/3). Both prior blind source readers judged B05 different. Controls B01 and P01 were preserved in all 3 draws of each arm. H01 and R05 changed in a source-supported direction 3/3 for independent versus 0/3 for both Jev arms; B10 differs by Jev request shape and draw. These are selected-case observations, not system precision or recall. Product change is not authorized or justified; stop this line, do not add cases or fit a follow-up prompt. Each result is being re-read independently and source-blind, with all 54 answers shuffled in `result-blind-packet.json`; council B reviews independently without sending extra experimental requests.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:73:Correction after Council B: the preregistered explicit stop controls named B01 and P01, not B05. The B05 3/3 vs 0/3 regression is a new serious finding and reason to stop, not an automatic predeclared stop trigger. Full raw evidence and the disagreement between fresh full versus single Jev remain disclosed in RESULTS-DRAFT.md.\nCOUNCIL-LOOP.md:75:Final council B complete: `results-codex.md`, `results-claude.md` and `results-codex-followup.md`. Both agree 54 calls completed, the comparator cannot be adopted, B05's source-backed regression is important, and it did **not** trip an explicitly predeclared B01/P01 stop condition. In 3/3 H01 the independent pair judgment matches the original announcement where full/single Jev miss it; in B05 the independent comparator answers supersedes 3/3 while Jev-single answers different 3/3 and Jev-full answers different once. R05's outcome is disputed: both initial source-only readers said different, but an arm-blind reader chose supersedes because the original publisher's later story is more cautious; a fresh output-blind source 
