ost to it.\n- Regression week ([results](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/results.md), `english-v34b-nvda-week-2026-10-27`, $0.23, 98 items, none failed): the whole path runs with the revision rule; `replacements` gains no row. Counts differ from the v18 week (129 against 176 evidence rows, 12 against 9 theses) because extraction is a sampler, not because of the writer; the writer's effect is proved on the decisions themselves. Reading the week's one `replace` decision found a second silent loss in the same code path: an incoming statement said before its target was logged in `late_statements` and linked nowhere (both weeks dropped SemiAnalysis's Kyber delay report this way; the three-month run dropped the SharonAI backstop figure; 1 of 3,216 decisions, each a material statement). Fixed in the same slice: an older statement is stored and linked as one more piece, no revision recorded, the log row kept. Test red on the old writer, green after; suite 209. Observed, not fixed here: 34 of 1,530 stored pieces carry a non-ISO `original_day` (\"2026-07-05 to 2026-07-06\", \"2026-03\"), which is what made the Kyber report \"older\"; an extraction-contract item for the next pass.\n\n## D203 · 2026-10-28 · A statement day is an ISO day or unknown; the writer never fills it with the publication day\n\n- Found while reading D202's regression week: the extraction answer's `original_day` is a free string (54 of the three-month run's 2,369 raw pieces carry a month, a range or text; 1,445 are empty) and the writer filled every empty day with the item's publication day, against D245's rule that an unknown stays unknown. A range read as \"older than\" the denial it answered dropped SemiAnalysis's Kyber delay report from the week ledger.\n- Decided, at the owners: `extraction.statement_day` keeps an ISO day and blanks anything else when the answer is sifted (the quote and `event_time` keep the period as written); `writing._store_piece` stores the stated day or '' and the revision path stores the stated day too (the ordering day `new_day` orders the revision only). Readers print the blank; matching's `said_day` still falls back to the publication day for ordering, never for storage. Tests: `test_a_statement_day_is_an_iso_day_or_unknown…` (red on the old sift), `test_an_unknown_statement_day_is_stored_unknown…` (red on the old writer); suite 211; preflight B/C/D unchanged.\n- The judge's revision note is labelled as what it is: \"Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of eX; both are in force\" (D202's census: 19 of 37 recorded revisions carry a wrong label).\n- Census of the other silent loss in the same path, read pair by pair ([labels](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/repeats-40-labels.json)): of 40 sampled `repeat` decisions (1,034 in the run), 32 are pickups, 8 merged a different or richer statement into an old piece and lost its content (an estimated 200 of 1,034). The mechanism is D202's: a one-sample label triggers an irreversible write (a repeat adds a source and discards the incoming text). The fix is the argument record's reader side (store every source record, relate `same_as`, collapse same-claim groups for the judge); not built here.\n- D201 measured further ([results](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/results.md), 2026-10-28 00:00–01:20, $0.85): a fresh 16-case gold written from the complete expansions before any send (action 11/12 and 4/4 held out; nothing wrongly retired 16/16; same-claim 8/12 with one class: a second outlet's own reporting treated as independent, which the contract could not express); arm 2 split claim identity from source independence (the class is gone; two new judgement weaknesses appeared); three draws per disagreeing case under both prompts show the arm-to-arm differences are within one draw's noise, while in 144 draws no must-not-touch piece was ever marked same or revised. Decided: the contract keeps arm 2's split; prompt arms stop here; the variable fields are annotations under D202 and the next build is the argument record (steps 5 and 6), where a wrong relation in one draw is corrected by the next instead of being frozen into the ledger.\n\n## D204 · 2026-10-28 · A repeat is stored as its own source record; the merge becomes a labelled relation\n\n- Alex: \"补那个洞，跑一周验收，仔细思考很重要\". The hole (D203's census): on a `repeat` decision the writer adds the incoming item as an outlet of the old piece and discards the incoming text; 8 of 40 sampled repeats (20%, about 200 of 1,034 in the run) had merged a different or richer statement, and its content was gone. The mechanism is D202's: a one-draw label (same_statement ≥ 0.5) triggers an irreversible write.\n- Choice weighed. (A) Store the incoming piece, link it to its own destinations, record the pair in `same_claims`, show both to the judge with the relation labelled as the matcher's opinion. (B) Keep the merge and store the text as a variant of the old piece, hidden from the judge. Under (A) true pickups (about 80%) appear twice in view for their first readings, labelled; under (B) the 20% wrong merges stay hidden from the judge. The standard (rule A: an outlet, not a fact; rule C: support counts sources) is served by the label; losing content is the failure that is not recoverable at read time. Decided: (A).\n- Decided: `writing` stores every incoming piece once with all its destination links; a `repeat` decision records (target, new, seq) in `same_claims`; the old piece gains no source row and no new link (the new piece carries the outlet and the links; a link written on a one-draw label is a write like any other). `store.evidence_in_force` carries `same_as` (the in-force pieces of its group); the judge's request prints \"Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as eX; the argument counts one claim\". Readers of `evidence`, `evidence_links` and `evidence_sources` keep their shapes; the library UI's per-row outlet count now counts one row's sources (the claim's outlets are its `same_claims` group), an open UI item.\n- Acceptance: tests red on the old writer (`test_a_repeated_statement_is_stored_as_its_own_record…`, the two D167 tests whose assertions pinned the merge, changed with this decision), a mutant that merges again fails them; the 40 sampled repeat decisions replayed through the new writer at $0 (40/40 stored, relation recorded, the 8 lost contents present); then one week through the whole path (`english-v34c-nvda-week`), counting `same_claims` rows, pairs both in the judge's view, and judgements citing both members of a pair (the double-count exposure the label must hold).\n- Accepted ([results](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/results.md)): 40 of 40 sampled repeat decisions replayed through the new writer keep the piece, the relation and both pieces in force (the 8 lost contents are present); the week through the whole path ran with none failed at $0.23, wrote 45 same-claim relations and no merge, and the judge's reasons where a pair was in view treat the relays as one source (\"ultimately trace to SemiAnalysis\", \"not independent confirmation\"). The three-month run may resume on `poc-v34` with D202–D204 in the writer; that is Alex's call.\n\n## D205 · 2026-10-28 · The judging call's output budget is 16,000 tokens\n\n- Found in the three-month resume (`english-v34-nvda-3m-2026-10-28`, 01:32): the judgement of v10 (Data Center revenue, a 24,150-token request) came back empty with `finish_reason` length: all 8,000 completion tokens were reasoning tokens, so the code read a malformed answer and the day halted (resumable; the re-send passed). Census over every archive: 2 of 793 judge answers hit the cap this way (the other in `english-v29-nvda-3m`, a 56k-token request), 13 of 793 used 6,000 or more. The archive books such a call at $0 while it costs its tokens (about $0.006 each).\n- Alex: \"嗯你加倍吧\". Decided: `rejudging.max_output_tokens` 8,000 → 16,000 in `poc-v34.json`, nothing else changed; a normal judgement costs the same, only a long-reasoning one may spend more. Applied from day 2026-07-22 of the run (days 1–21 ran under 8,000; the archive records the configuration checksum per call).\n- Also from this run: the Mac slept at about 02:00 and a Jev call failed with URLError during a dark wake; the run's `launch.sh` now wraps the run in `caffeinate -i -s`.\n\n\n## D206 · 2026-10-28 · Every open theme thesis is shown to every item's extraction (extraction v19, `poc-v35`)\n\n- Alex: \"你可以改A然后尝试\". The class ($0, `docs/research/2026-10-28-extraction-quality/report.md`): every one of the run's 1,414 extraction requests named the H200 key in its reference list while the H200 thesis (a theme) was never in the shown list; 48 pieces linked only to theme ids the groups block printed and the link check refused; three H200 theses opened for one matter.\n- Decided: `store.views_for_prompt(themes=True)` lists every open theme thesis after the objects' own, in creation order; `extraction.shown_views` is the one owner of the shown list (the stream and the parallel runner both read it); the groups block prints only member ids the answer may link to. Gated on the prompt version (`THEMES_SHOWN_FROM = 19`): v18 requests are byte-for-byte as before.\n- Measured: frozen gold (`gold-standard.md`, 26 articles, 26 statements, 11 core; `ab_gold.py`): control (production bytes, 26/26 identities archived) 9/11/7 kept right against the arm's 13/15/14 over three sends, core 6/6/5 → 9/8/8, written-dropped 13/12/13 → 8/7/8, extra flat; two weeks through the whole path (`english-v35-nvda-2w-2026-10-28`, $0.59): one H200 thesis instead of three, 14 pieces and 3 judgements on it, capex themes 7 pieces / 4–5 judgements each against 2 / 2, zero drops for an unshown id (17 in the control weeks). Tests `tests/test_theme_shown.py`.\n\n## D207 · 2026-10-28 · Statements are filed by a separate placement call under the one-home rule; an unfiled statement is kept (extraction v20, `poc-v36`)\n\n- Alex, on the root cause (\"你还是没有根因的去解决这个问题 … 要么挂不到，要么挂多\"; \"跑那个归档实验\"; \"你看着结果来做\"; \"一样的标准开始测\"). The mechanism ([routing-analysis.md](research/2026-10-28-extraction-quality/routing-analysis.md)): the in-call link decision was a coin flip (36% right on the gold, 46–78 pieces kept from the same bytes) and the gate at once (an unlinked statement was dropped: 60% of all statements, ~15–30% of them material); the link rule routed demand news to the company-wide quantities (six root theses held 66% of all links; v2's pieces 86% double-linked, 26% cited); the thesis list had no driver layer.\n- Decided, three parts measured one at a time on the frozen gold (three draws each, 8 threads, $0.04–0.05 an arm) and on the first week's 255 in-call pieces: (1) `placement.py`: one call per item with the title line, the statements and the open questions, each with a code-written 'takes' line (key, event type, research-group names; aggregates admit other populations); the sift keeps statements without a link (`keep_unlinked`); the placer's links replace the extraction's, candidate links survive; a statement filed nowhere is stored in `unplaced_statements` with the handover. (2) The rule is the placement prompt: `placement-narrow-v1` — one home, the narrowest question; company-wide figure questions take only their own figures, guidance and management statements. (3) D42's \"evidence is linked at extraction\" becomes: the extraction's links are its first opinion; placement decides. Gated on the prompt version (`PLACEMENT_FROM = 20`); `cfg.placement` is required from v20.\n- Measured: core statements filed right 6/6/5 → 9/9/9 (with six seeded driver questions shown) and 9/10/9 under the old rule; wrong links 9 → 3; links to the two sinks 63/60/44 → 6/1/5; junk placed 53/48/32 → 39/27/35; every decisive matter statement (the Kyber/Rubin Ultra rack delay cluster, the AI Compute Partnership participants, Goldman's capex estimate) placed; one week through the whole path (`english-v36-nvda-1w-2026-10-28`, $0.22 against $0.22) kept 580 statements the old path dropped. Arms retired by measurement: the extraction's links shown as a hint (junk and sink links returned), group aliases alone (the groups lack the press names). Tests `tests/test_placement.py`, suite 222.\n- Not built here: re-placement of unplaced statements when a thesis opens later (the cold-start class, 12% of gold cells); the driver layer (D208).\n\n## D208 · 2026-10-28 · The thesis tree: root quantities, a seeded driver layer per company, shared macro themes with declared channels (design, not built)","numLines":45,"startLine":2594,"totalLines":4365}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018CmcTqdQF4YFPwjfG4kVSv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/claude-independent.jsonl:43:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SxVuhpA2vDmTFvogzGfGiq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Isolated Step 2 for the clean path (PRD §5): search the entity's stored evidence for each {thesis, incoming evidence} association,\n2\task Jev how the incoming evidence relates to each candidate, and turn the answers into the outcome Step 3 writes.\n3\t\n4\tSearch: one query per association (the thesis question, then the incoming summary and passages) against each group's original record\n5\t(summary, passages, party, statement date, period), cosine similarity of embeddings, top 10; a record with no association, or one that\n6\tlists the company's figures (a condition), also gets one entity-wide query of its own text (STEP1-CONDITIONS-DESIGN.md §10.1); the union\n7\tof the results is compared. The figures never enter a search or comparison text, so a wrongly paired figure cannot change Step 2 (§14);\n8\tthe comparison reads the full passages (§15). Comparison: Jev's piece question with the production criteria (views/jev_matching), the incoming piece as state, one question\n9\tper candidate. Outcome: any same_statement makes the record a repeat of the candidate with the highest same_statement probability, ties\n10\tgoing to the earliest group (Alex, 2026-11-08: only the group it is most like); a supersedes answer on another candidate becomes a\n11\trevision link; with no same_statement, supersedes answers make it a revision of those groups; otherwise it is new.\n12\t\n13\t`forward` runs articles in order against the library as it stood after the previous article: records of one article never see each\n14\tother. A failed comparison is refused by the library, reported, and the run continues.\"\"\"\n15\timport concurrent.futures\n16\timport math\n17\timport sys\n18\tfrom pathlib import Path\n19\t\n20\tROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n21\tsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / 'src'))\n22\tfrom hivemind.views import jev_matching  # noqa: E402\n23\t\n24\tTOP = 10\n25\t\n26\t\n27\tdef stated(record):\n28\t    return record['statement_date'] or record.get('statement_date_text') or 'unknown'\n29\t\n30\t\n31\tdef doc_text(record):\n32\t    return '\\n'.join([record['summary'], ' '.join(record['passages']), f\"party: {record['original_party'] or 'unknown'}\",\n33\t                      f\"stated: {stated(record)}\", f\"period: {record['evidence_period'] or 'unknown'}\"])\n34\t\n35\t\n36\tdef query_text(record, thesis_question):\n37\t    return f\"thesis: {thesis_question}\\n{record['summary']}\\n{' '.join(record['passages'])}\"\n38\t\n39\t\n40\tdef piece_text(record, label):\n41\t    return (f\"{label} [{record['tier']}; {record['reporting_speaker']}; original source {record['original_party']}, stated \"\n42\t            f\"{stated(record)}] {record['summary']} | quote: {' '.join(record['passages'])}\")\n43\t\n44\t\n45\tdef query_vectors(vectors, record, thesis_questions):\n46\t    \"\"\"The search queries of one record, in order: one per thesis association, then its own text when it has no association or lists\n47\t    the company's figures.\"\"\"\n48\t    queries = [vectors[query_text(record, thesis_questions[t])] for t in record['thesis_ids']]\n49\t    if not record['thesis_ids'] or record.get('figures'):\n50\t        queries.append(vectors[doc_text(record)])\n51\t    return queries\n52\t\n53\t\n54\t# Jev's piece criteria aligned with the Step 2 merge line's own test (PRD §5 line 2; AGENTS §7.1, one ruler): a repeat is a later report\n55\t# of the stored piece's main statement. Production's wording (views/jev_matching.PIECES) judged \"the same evidence\", so a later report of\n56\t# only a secondary statement inside a stored record (an official's denial carried in the report it denies) was merged as a repeat.\n57\tPIECES = {'same_statement': \"the INCOMING PIECE reports the STORED PIECE's main statement: a retelling, another outlet carrying it, the \"\n58\t                            \"same number in text or a table, or the same speaker repeating it; wording, precision and extra detail may \"\n59\t                            \"differ. If the stored piece carries several statements and the incoming piece reports only a secondary one, \"\n60\t                            \"this is not it\",\n61\t          'supersedes': \"a later version of the stored piece's main statement, changed: the same speaker revises that guidance, \"\n62\t                        \"forecast or event-progress statement, an official confirms or denies that reported claim, or the original \"\n63\t                        \"source revises it; another statement on the same topic is not this\",\n64\t          'different': \"a different fact, figure or matter, a figure for another period or quantity, or only a secondary statement of \"\n65\t                       \"the stored piece, even if on the same topic\"}\n66\t\n67\t\n68\tdef piece_question(text):\n69\t    return {'type': 'choice', 'criteria': PIECES,\n70\t            'instructions': 'How does the INCOMING PIECE relate to the STORED PIECE below? Use only the supplied text. STORED PIECE:\\n' + text}\n71\t\n72\t\n73\tINFORMS = {'true': \"the STORED PIECE bears on the THESIS's own matter (the parties, products, policy or quantity the THESIS names) and \"\n74\t                   \"makes its answer more or less likely, as evidence filed under it would\",\n75\t           'false': \"the STORED PIECE concerns another matter, or is a company-wide result or event that does not speak to the THESIS's \"\n76\t                    \"own matter, or would not change its answer\"}\n77\t\n78\t\n79\tdef informs_question(text):\n80\t    return {'type': 'noul', 'criteria': INFORMS,\n81\t            'instructions': 'Does the STORED PIECE below inform the THESIS stated above? Use only the supplied text; a shared company, '\n82\t                            'product family or word is not enough, and the company\\'s overall results, guidance and estimates inform a '\n83\t                            'thesis about its revenue or earnings path, not one about a competitor, a supplier or a policy unless they '\n84\t                            'speak to it. STORED PIECE:\\n' + text}\n85\t\n86\t\n87\tdef later_link_judge(library, thesis_question, ask):\n88\t    \"\"\"The judge `Library.link_later` calls: one Jev request per batch, the thesis as state, one yes/no question per stored group.\"\"\"\n89\t    def judge(group_ids):\n90\t        questions = {f'q{i}': informs_question(piece_text(library.groups[g]['original'], 'STORED PIECE')) for i, g in enumerate(group_ids)}\n91\t        raw = ask(f'THESIS: {thesis_question}', questions)\n92\t        return {g: raw[f'q{i}']['noul'] >= jev_matching.THRESHOLD for i, g in enumerate(group_ids)}\n93\t    return judge\n94\t\n95\t\n96\tdef cosine(a, b):\n97\t    return sum(x * y for x, y in zip(a, b)) / (math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in a)) * math.sqrt(sum(y * y for y in b)) or 1)\n98\t\n99\t\n100\tdef search(library, vectors, record, thesis_questions):\n101\t    \"\"\"Candidate group ids: each query's top 10 by cosine against the groups' original records, merged in rank order.\"\"\"\n102\t    candidates = []\n103\t    for query in query_vectors(vectors, record, thesis_questions):\n104\t        ranked = sorted(library.order, key=lambda g: -cosine(query, vectors[doc_text(library.groups[g]['original'])]))[:TOP]\n105\t        candidates += [g for g in ranked if g not in candidates]\n106\t    return candidates\n107\t\n108\t\n109\tdef outcome(answers, order):\n110\t    \"\"\"answers: {group id: {'choice', 'probabilities'}}; order: group ids in creation order.\"\"\"\n111\t    same = [g for g, a in answers.items() if a['choice'] == 'same_statement']\n112\t    later = [g for g, a in answers.items() if a['choice'] == 'supersedes']\n113\t    if same:\n114\t        best = max(same, key=lambda g: (answers[g]['probabilities']['same_statement'], -order.index(g)))\n115\t        return {'kind': 'repeat', 'repeat_of': [best], 'revises': later}\n116\t    if later:\n117\t        return {'kind': 'revision', 'revises': later}\n118\t    return {'kind': 'new'}\n119\t\n120\t\n121\tdef forward(articles, library, vectors, thesis_questions, ask, workers=8, opened=None):\n122\t    \"\"\"articles: lists of Step 3 records in article order. ask(state, questions) returns Jev's answers by question id, or raises.\n123\t    opened: per article, the thesis ids it opened; after the article's records are written, each is linked later to the stored groups\n124\t    that arrived unlinked from earlier articles (`Library.link_later`). A thesis written to with pairs still pending is judged again,\n125\t    against its opening boundary. Returns one decision per record.\"\"\"\n126\t    decisions = []\n127\t    for index, records in enumerate(articles):\n128\t        def decide(record):\n129\t            candidates = search(library, vectors, record, thesis_questions)\n130\t            if not candidates:\n131\t                return record, candidates, {}, {'kind': 'new'}\n132\t            questions = {f'q{i}': piece_question(piece_text(library.groups[g]['original'], 'STORED PIECE'))\n133\t                         for i, g in enumerate(candidates)}\n134\t            incoming = piece_text(record, 'INCOMING PIECE')\n135\t            try:\n136\t                raw = ask(incoming, questions)\n137\t            except Exception as first:   # retried once; a second failure is reported, never silently saved as new\n138\t                try:\n139\t                    raw = ask(incoming, questions)\n140\t                except Exception as error:\n141\t                    return record, candidates, {}, {'kind': 'failed', 'reason': f'{type(first).__name__}: {first}; retry: {type(error).__name__}: {error}'}\n142\t            answers = {g: {'choice': raw[f'q{i}']['choice'], 'probabilities': raw[f'q{i}']['probabilities']} for i, g in enumerate(candidates)}\n143\t            return record, candidates, answers, outcome(answers, library.order)\n144\t        with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=workers) as pool:\n145\t            results = list(pool.map(decide, records))\n146\t        for record, candidates, answers, result in results:\n147\t            entry = {'id': record['id'], 'candidates': candidates, 'answers': answers, 'outcome': result}\n148\t            try:\n149\t                entry['group'] = library.apply(record, result)\n150\t            except Exception as error:\n151\t                entry['refused'] = f'{type(error).__name__}: {error}'\n152\t            decisions.append(entry)\n153\t        article = records[0]['article'] if records else None\n154\t        if article is None:\n155\t            continue\n156\t        written = {t for r in records for t in r['thesis_ids']}\n157\t        retry = [t for t in written if t in library.pending and t not in (opened[index] if opened else [])]\n158\t        for thesis_id in list(opened[index] if opened else []) + retry:   # opened here, or written to with pairs still pending\n159\t            result = library.link_later(thesis_id, later_link_judge(library, thesis_questions[thesis_id], ask), article)\n160\t            library.later_log.append({'thesis': thesis_id, 'article': article, **result})\n161\t    return decisions\n162\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78ccad56-ed8d-4e29-91b7-f576c6d2916d","uuid":"d38a8f20-42bd-4a03-8a32-01a393032ffb","timestamp":"2026-11-09T21:06:40.248Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2/compare.py","content":"\"\"\"Isolated Step 2 for the clean path (PRD §5): search the entity's stored evidence for each {thesis, incoming evidence} association,\nask Jev how the incoming evidence relates to each candidate, and turn the answers into the outcome Step 3 writes.\n\nSearch: one query per association (the thesis question, then the incoming summary and passages) against each group's original record\n(summary, passages, party, statement date, period), cosine similarity of embeddings, top 10; a record with no association, or one that\nlists the company's figures (a condition), also gets one entity-wide query of its own text (STEP1-CONDITIONS-DESIGN.md §10.1); the union\nof the results is compared. The figures never enter a search or comparison text, so a wrongly paired figure cannot change Step 2 (§14);\nthe comparison reads the full passages (§15). Comparison: Jev's piece question with the production criteria (views/jev_matching), the incoming piece as state, one question\nper candidate. Outcome: any same_statement makes the record a repeat of the candidate with the highest same_statement probability, ties\ngoing to the earliest group (Alex, 2026-11-08: only the group it is most like); a supersedes answer on another candidate becomes a\nrevision link; with no same_statement, supersedes answers make it a revision of those groups; otherwise it is new.\n\n`forward` runs articles in order against the library as it stood after the previous article: records of one article never see each\nother. A failed comparison is refused by the library, reported, and the run continues.\"\"\"\nimport concurrent.futures\nimport math\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / 'src'))\nfrom hivemind.views import jev_matching  # noqa: E402\n\nTOP = 10\n\n\ndef stated(record):\n    return record['statement_date'] or record.get('statement_date_text') or 'unknown'\n\n\ndef doc_text(record):\n    return '\\n'.join([record['summary'], ' '.join(record['passages']), f\"party: {record['original_party'] or 'unknown'}\",\n                      f\"stated: {stated(record)}\", f\"period: {record['evidence_period'] or 'unknown'}\"])\n\n\ndef query_text(record, thesis_question):\n    return f\"thesis: {thesis_question}\\n{record['summary']}\\n{' '.join(record['passages'])}\"\n\n\ndef piece_text(record, label):\n    return (f\"{label} [{record['tier']}; {record['reporting_speaker']}; original source {record['original_party']}, stated \"\n            f\"{stated(record)}] {record['summary']} | quote: {' '.join(record['passages'])}\")\n\n\ndef query_vectors(vectors, record, thesis_questions):\n    \"\"\"The search queries of one record, in order: one per thesis association, then its own text when it has no association or lists\n    the company's figures.\"\"\"\n    queries = [vectors[query_text(record, thesis_questions[t])] for t in record['thesis_ids']]\n    if not record['thesis_ids'] or record.get('figures'):\n        queries.append(vectors[doc_text(record)])\n    return queries\n\n\n# Jev's piece criteria aligned with the Step 2 merge line's own test (PRD §5 line 2; AGENTS §7.1, one ruler): a repeat is a later report\n# of the stored piece's main statement. Production's wording (views/jev_matching.PIECES) judged \"the same evidence\", so a later report of\n# only a secondary statement inside a stored record (an official's denial carried in the report it denies) was merged as a repeat.\nPIECES = {'same_statement': \"the INCOMING PIECE reports the STORED PIECE's main statement: a retelling, another outlet carrying it, the \"\n                            \"same number in text or a table, or the same speaker repeating it; wording, precision and extra detail may \"\n                            \"differ. If the stored piece carries several statements and the incoming piece reports only a secondary one, \"\n                            \"this is not it\",\n          'supersedes': \"a later version of the stored piece's main statement, changed: the same speaker revises that guidance, \"\n                        \"forecast or event-progress statement, an official confirms or denies that reported claim, or the original \"\n                        \"source revises it; another statement on the same topic is not this\",\n          'different': \"a different fact, figure or matter, a figure for another period or quantity, or only a secondary statement of \"\n                       \"the stored piece, even if on the same topic\"}\n\n\ndef piece_question(text):\n    return {'type': 'choice', 'criteria': PIECES,\n            'instructions': 'How does the INCOMING PIECE relate to the STORED PIECE below? Use only the supplied text. STORED PIECE:\\n' + text}\n\n\nINFORMS = {'true': \"the STORED PIECE bears on the THESIS's own matter (the parties, products, policy or quantity the THESIS names) and \"\n                   \"makes its answer more or less likely, as evidence filed under it would\",\n           'false': \"the STORED PIECE concerns another matter, or is a company-wide result or event that does not speak to the THESIS's \"\n                    \"own matter, or would not change its answer\"}\n\n\ndef informs_question(text):\n    return {'type': 'noul', 'criteria': INFORMS,\n            'instructions': 'Does the STORED PIECE below inform the THESIS stated above? Use only the supplied text; a shared company, '\n                            'product family or word is not enough, and the company\\'s overall results, guidance and estimates inform a '\n                            'thesis about its revenue or earnings path, not one about a competitor, a supplier or a policy unless they '\n                            'speak to it. STORED PIECE:\\n' + text}\n\n\ndef later_link_judge(library, thesis_question, ask):\n    \"\"\"The judge `Library.link_later` calls: one Jev request per batch, the thesis as state, one yes/no question per stored group.\"\"\"\n    def judge(group_ids):\n        questions = {f'q{i}': informs_question(piece_text(library.groups[g]['original'], 'STORED PIECE')) for i, g in enumerate(group_ids)}\n        raw = ask(f'THESIS: {thesis_question}', questions)\n        return {g: raw[f'q{i}']['noul'] >= jev_matching.THRESHOLD for i, g in enumerate(group_ids)}\n    return judge\n\n\ndef cosine(a, b):\n    return sum(x * y for x, y in zip(a, b)) / (math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in a)) * math.sqrt(sum(y * y for y in b)) or 1)\n\n\ndef search(library, vectors, record, thesis_questions):\n    \"\"\"Candidate group ids: each query's top 10 by cosine against the groups' original records, merged in rank order.\"\"\"\n    candidates = []\n    for query in query_vectors(vectors, record, thesis_questions):\n        ranked = sorted(library.order, key=lambda g: -cosine(query, vectors[doc_text(library.groups[g]['original'])]))[:TOP]\n        candidates += [g for g in ranked if g not in candidates]\n    return candidates\n\n\ndef outcome(answers, order):\n    \"\"\"answers: {group id: {'choice', 'probabilities'}}; order: group ids in creation order.\"\"\"\n    same = [g for g, a in answers.items() if a['choice'] == 'same_statement']\n    later = [g for g, a in answers.items() if a['choice'] == 'supersedes']\n    if same:\n        best = max(same, key=lambda g: (answers[g]['probabilities']['same_statement'], -order.index(g)))\n        return {'kind': 'repeat', 'repeat_of': [best], 'revises': later}\n    if later:\n        return {'kind': 'revision', 'revises': later}\n    return {'kind': 'new'}\n\n\ndef forward(articles, library, vectors, thesis_questions, ask, workers=8, opened=None):\n    \"\"\"articles: lists of Step 3 records in article order. ask(state, questions) returns Jev's answers by question id, or raises.\n    opened: per article, the thesis ids it opened; after the article's records are written, each is linked later to the stored groups\n    that arrived unlinked from earlier articles (`Library.link_later`). A thesis written to with pairs still pending is judged again,\n    against its opening boundary. Returns one decision per record.\"\"\"\n    decisions = []\n    for index, records in enumerate(articles):\n        def decide(record):\n            candidates = search(library, vectors, record, thesis_questions)\n            if not candidates:\n                return record, candidates, {}, {'kind': 'new'}\n            questions = {f'q{i}': piece_question(piece_text(library.groups[g]['original'], 'STORED PIECE'))\n                         for i, g in enumerate(candidates)}\n            incoming = piece_text(record, 'INCOMING PIECE')\n            try:\n                raw = ask(incoming, questions)\n            except Exception as first:   # retried once; a second failure is reported, never silently saved as new\n                try:\n                    raw = ask(incoming, questions)\n                except Exception as error:\n                    return record, candidates, {}, {'kind': 'failed', 'reason': f'{type(first).__name__}: {first}; retry: {type(error).__name__}: {error}'}\n            answers = {g: {'choice': raw[f'q{i}']['choice'], 'probabilities': raw[f'q{i}']['probabilities']} for i, g in enumerate(candidates)}\n            return record, candidates, answers, outcome(answers, library.order)\n        with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=workers) as pool:\n            results = list(pool.map(decide, records))\n        for record, candidates, answers, result in results:\n            entry = {'id': record['id'], 'candidates': candidates, 'answers': answers, 'outcome': result}\n            try:\n                entry['group'] = library.apply(record, result)\n            except Exception as error:\n                entry['refused'] = f'{type(error).__name__}: {error}'\n            decisions.append(entry)\n        article = records[0]['article'] if records else None\n        if article is None:\n            continue\n        written = {t for r in records for t in r['thesis_ids']}\n        retry = [t for t in written if t in library.pending and t not in (opened[index] if opened else [])]\n        for thesis_id in list(opened[index] if opened else []) + retry:   # opened here, or written to with pairs still pending\n            result = library.link_later(thesis_id, later_link_judge(library, thesis_questions[thesis_id], ask), article)\n            library.later_log.append({'thesis': thesis_id, 'article': article, **result})\n    return decisions\n","numLines":162,"startLine":1,"totalLines":162}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SxVuhpA2vDmTFvogzGfGiq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
reports/step2-jev-decision-council-2026-11-09/claude-independent.jsonl:45:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HWTKjWvouUzJFbUTqWRGVF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Isolated Step 3 evidence library for the clean path (PRD §6): an in-memory logical store and its dossier text, not the live writer.\n2\t\n3\tA group is one stored statement. Its original record keeps its id and fields unchanged and gives the group its id. A later record that\n4\tStep 2 judged a repeat joins the group as a member and keeps its own id, text, fields and source article. Thesis links belong to the\n5\tgroup and remember the record that brought each one. A revision is its own group, linked to every group it revises; a repeat that also\n6\trevises another group adds that link to its own group, naming the member that established it.\n7\t\n8\tThe writer refuses rather than guesses: a failed comparison, several repeat targets, an unknown group, or a replayed record whose\n9\tplacement differs from the first time raise `Refused` and write nothing. Physical storage and crash recovery are not provided here.\n10\t\n11\tLater linking (Alex, 2026-11-08: a material statement no thesis takes is kept and linked when a related thesis opens; design\n12\tSTEP1-CONDITIONS-DESIGN.md §§11.1, 17): when a thesis opens, every group whose original arrived with no link, from an earlier article,\n13\tis judged against it in batches. Each judged (thesis, group) pair is recorded once in `judged`; a batch that fails twice stays pending,\n14\tis reported, and is judged again on the next write to that thesis, against the same opening boundary (`opened_at`).\"\"\"\n15\timport copy\n16\t\n17\tRECORD_FIELDS = ('id', 'article', 'publisher', 'publication_date', 'summary', 'passages', 'original_party', 'reporting_speaker', 'tier',\n18\t                 'statement_date', 'evidence_period', 'thesis_ids')\n19\t\n20\t\n21\tclass Refused(Exception):\n22\t    \"\"\"A Step 2 outcome the library will not write; nothing was changed.\"\"\"\n23\t\n24\t\n25\tclass Library:\n26\t    def __init__(self):\n27\t        self.groups = {}       # group id → {'original': record, 'members': [record], 'links': {thesis id: record id}, 'revises': [{'group', 'by'}]}\n28\t        self.placement = {}    # record id → group id\n29\t        self.order = []        # group ids in the order they were created\n30\t        self.judged = {}       # (thesis id, group id) → True | False, the later-linking ledger\n31\t        self.later_log = []    # one entry per later-linking call: thesis, article, linked, pending, judged\n32\t        self.opened_at = {}    # thesis id → the article that opened it: the boundary of its later linking\n33\t        self.pending = {}      # thesis id → group ids whose judgement failed twice and waits for the next write to the thesis\n34\t\n35\t    def apply(self, record, outcome):\n36\t        \"\"\"Write one record with its Step 2 outcome: {'kind': 'new' | 'repeat' | 'revision' | 'failed', 'repeat_of': [group ids],\n37\t        'revises': [group ids], 'reason': text}. Returns the id of the group that holds the record.\"\"\"\n38\t        missing = [f for f in RECORD_FIELDS if f not in record]\n39\t        if missing:\n40\t            raise Refused(f'record lacks {missing}')\n41\t        kind, repeat_of, revises = outcome['kind'], list(outcome.get('repeat_of') or []), list(outcome.get('revises') or [])\n42\t        if kind == 'failed':\n43\t            raise Refused(f\"comparison failed for {record['id']}: {outcome.get('reason', 'no reason given')}\")\n44\t        if kind not in ('new', 'repeat', 'revision'):\n45\t            raise Refused(f'unknown outcome {kind!r}')\n46\t        if (kind == 'repeat') != bool(repeat_of) or len(repeat_of) > 1:\n47\t            raise Refused(f\"a repeat names exactly one group; got {repeat_of} for outcome {kind}\")\n48\t        if kind == 'revision' and not revises:\n49\t            raise Refused('a revision names the group it revises')\n50\t        for group_id in repeat_of + revises:\n51\t            if group_id not in self.groups:\n52\t                raise Refused(f'unknown group {group_id}')\n53\t        target = repeat_of[0] if repeat_of else record['id']\n54\t        if record['id'] in self.placement:\n55\t            if self.placement[record['id']] != target:\n56\t                raise Refused(f\"{record['id']} was placed in {self.placement[record['id']]}, not {target}\")\n57\t            group = self.groups[target]\n58\t            stored = next(r for r in [group['original']] + group['members'] if r['id'] == record['id'])\n59\t            if {k: v for k, v in stored.items() if k != 'thesis_ids'} != {k: v for k, v in record.items() if k != 'thesis_ids'}:\n60\t                raise Refused(f\"{record['id']} names a stored record with different content; a changed record needs a new id\")\n61\t            self._link(group, record)\n62\t            return target\n63\t        if kind == 'repeat':\n64\t            group = self.groups[target]\n65\t            group['members'].append(copy.deepcopy(record))\n66\t        else:\n67\t            group = {'original': copy.deepcopy(record), 'members': [], 'links': {}, 'revises': []}\n68\t            self.groups[target] = group\n69\t            self.order.append(target)\n70\t        self.placement[record['id']] = target\n71\t        self._link(group, record)\n72\t        for revised in revises:\n73\t            if revised != target and not any(r['group'] == revised for r in group['revises']):\n74\t                group['revises'].append({'group': revised, 'by': record['id']})\n75\t        return target\n76\t\n77\t    def link_later(self, thesis_id, judge, before_article, batch=10):\n78\t        \"\"\"Judge every group whose original arrived unlinked from an article before `before_article` against a newly opened thesis.\n79\t        judge(group ids) returns {group id: True | False} or raises. Returns {'linked': [...], 'pending': [...], 'judged': n}.\"\"\"\n80\t        self.opened_at.setdefault(thesis_id, before_article)\n81\t        before_article = self.opened_at[thesis_id]\n82\t        todo = [g for g in self.order if not self.groups[g]['original']['thesis_ids']\n83\t                and self.groups[g]['original']['article'] < before_article and (thesis_id, g) not in self.judged]\n84\t        linked, pending = [], []\n85\t        for start in range(0, len(todo), batch):\n86\t            ids = todo[start:start + batch]\n87\t            answers = None\n88\t            for _attempt in range(2):\n89\t                try:\n90\t                    answers = judge(ids)\n91\t                    break\n92\t                except Exception:   # tried twice, then reported as pending, never saved as a judgement\n93\t                    answers = None\n94\t            if answers is None:\n95\t                pending += ids\n96\t                continue\n97\t            for group_id in ids:\n98\t                self.judged[(thesis_id, group_id)] = bool(answers[group_id])\n99\t                if answers[group_id]:\n100\t                    self.groups[group_id]['links'].setdefault(thesis_id, self.groups[group_id]['original']['id'])\n101\t                    linked.append(group_id)\n102\t        if pending:\n103\t            self.pending[thesis_id] = pending\n104\t        else:\n105\t            self.pending.pop(thesis_id, None)\n106\t        return {'linked': linked, 'pending': pending, 'judged': len(todo) - len(pending)}\n107\t\n108\t    @staticmethod\n109\t    def _link(group, record):\n110\t        for thesis_id in record['thesis_ids']:\n111\t            group['links'].setdefault(thesis_id, record['id'])\n112\t\n113\t    @staticmethod\n114\t    def articles(group):\n115\t        \"\"\"Distinct source articles of a group, oldest first; two records from one article count once.\"\"\"\n116\t        seen = []\n117\t        for record in [group['original']] + group['members']:\n118\t            if record['article'] not in seen:\n119\t                seen.append(record['article'])\n120\t        return seen\n121\t\n122\t    def dossier(self, thesis_id):\n123\t        \"\"\"Group ids linked to a thesis, in creation order.\"\"\"\n124\t        return [g for g in self.order if thesis_id in self.groups[g]['links']]\n125\t\n126\t\n127\tdef labelled_passages(record):\n128\t    \"\"\"Each passage as a reader sees it: the source text Step 1 found, labelled 'Quote', or, when Step 1 did not find it (verified\n129\t    value None), the model's text labelled 'Unverified quote'. The model's own text stays in the record's `passages`. A record stored\n130\t    before verification was carried shows its passages as 'Quote'.\"\"\"\n131\t    verified = record.get('verified_passages') or record['passages']\n132\t    return [('Quote', found) if found is not None else ('Unverified quote', passage) for passage, found in zip(record['passages'], verified)]\n133\t\n134\t\n135\tdef record_text(record, label):\n136\t    attribution = record['original_party'] or 'unknown party'\n137\t    if record['reporting_speaker'] and record['reporting_speaker'] != record['original_party']:\n138\t        attribution += f\", reported by {record['reporting_speaker']}\"\n139\t    head = (f\"[{label}] {record['publication_date']} · {record['publisher'] or 'unknown publisher'} · {attribution} · tier {record['tier']}\"\n140\t            f\" · stated {record['statement_date'] or 'unknown'} · period {record['evidence_period'] or 'unknown'}\")\n141\t    quotes = '\\n'.join(f'  {label_of}: \"{p}\"' for label_of, p in labelled_passages(record))\n142\t    return f\"{head}\\n  {record['summary']}\\n{quotes}\"\n143\t\n144\t\n145\tdef group_text(library, group_id, label, labels, member_text=True, notes=()):\n146\t    \"\"\"A group as a reader sees it: the original record, then each later report of the same statement in arrival order, with its own\n147\t    text when `member_text` is set and as a source line otherwise. Distinct articles are counted; repeats are not called confirmation.\"\"\"\n148\t    group = library.groups[group_id]\n149\t    lines = [record_text(group['original'], label)]\n150\t    if group['members']:\n151\t        articles = library.articles(group)\n152\t        publishers = {r['publisher'] for r in [group['original']] + group['members']}\n153\t        lines.append(f'  Later reports of the same statement: {len(group[\"members\"])} records from {len(articles) - 1} further articles '\n154\t                     f'({len(publishers)} publishers in all). Articles repeating a statement do not by themselves confirm it independently.')\n155\t        for member in group['members']:\n156\t            if member_text:\n157\t                party = '' if member['original_party'] == group['original']['original_party'] else f\" · {member['original_party']}\"\n158\t                quotes = ' '.join(f'\"{p}\"' if kind == 'Quote' else f'\"{p}\" (unverified)' for kind, p in labelled_passages(member))\n159\t                lines.append(f\"    - {member['publication_date']} · {member['publisher']}{party}: {member['summary']}\\n      Quote: {quotes}\")\n160\t            else:\n161\t                lines.append(f\"    - {member['publication_date']} · {member['publisher']}\")\n162\t    for revised in group['revises']:\n163\t        lines.append(f\"  Revises [{labels[revised['group']]}].\" if revised['group'] in labels else '  Revises an entry outside this dossier.')\n164\t    lines += [f'  {note}' for note in notes]\n165\t    return '\\n'.join(lines)\n166\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78ccad56-ed8d-4e29-91b7-f576c6d2916d","uuid":"8a4202dc-d85d-4af6-92e4-5aae45f57305","timestamp":"2026-11-09T21:06:40.723Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step3/library.py","content":"\"\"\"Isolated Step 3 evidence library for the clean path (PRD §6): an in-memory logical store and its dossier text, not the live writer.\n\nA group is one stored statement. Its original record keeps its id and fields unchanged and gives the group its id. A later record that\nStep 2 judged a repeat joins the group as a member and keeps its own id, text, fields and source article. Thesis links belong to the\ngroup and remember the record that brought each one. A revision is its own group, linked to every group it revises; a repeat that also\nrevises another group adds that link to its own group, naming the member that established it.\n\nThe writer refuses rather than guesses: a failed comparison, several repeat targets, an unknown group, or a replayed record whose\nplacement differs from the first time raise `Refused` and write nothing. Physical storage and crash recovery are not provided here.\n\nLater linking (Alex, 2026-11-08: a material statement no thesis takes is kept and linked when a related thesis opens; design\nSTEP1-CONDITIONS-DESIGN.md §§11.1, 17): when a thesis opens, every group whose original arrived with no link, from an earlier article,\nis judged against it in batches. Each judged (thesis, group) pair is recorded once in `judged`; a batch that fails twice stays pending,\nis reported, and is judged again on the next write to that thesis, against the same opening boundary (`opened_at`).\"\"\"\nimport copy\n\nRECORD_FIELDS = ('id', 'article', 'publisher', 'publication_date', 'summary', 'passages', 'original_party', 'reporting_speaker', 'tier',\n                 'statement_date', 'evidence_period', 'thesis_ids')\n\n\nclass Refused(Exception):\n    \"\"\"A Step 2 outcome the library will not write; nothing was changed.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass Library:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.groups = {}       # group id → {'original': record, 'members': [record], 'links': {thesis id: record id}, 'revises': [{'group', 'by'}]}\n        self.placement = {}    # record id → group id\n        self.order = []        # group ids in the order they were created\n        self.judged = {}       # (thesis id, group id) → True | False, the later-linking ledger\n        self.later_log = []    # one entry per later-linking call: thesis, article, linked, pending, judged\n        self.opened_at = {}    # thesis id → the article that opened it: the boundary of its later linking\n        self.pending = {}      # thesis id → group ids whose judgement failed twice and waits for the next write to the thesis\n\n    def apply(self, record, outcome):\n        \"\"\"Write one record with its Step 2 outcome: {'kind': 'new' | 'repeat' | 'revision' | 'failed', 'repeat_of': [group ids],\n        'revises': [group ids], 'reason': text}. Returns the id of the group that holds the record.\"\"\"\n        missing = [f for f in RECORD_FIELDS if f not in record]\n        if missing:\n            raise Refused(f'record lacks {missing}')\n        kind, repeat_of, revises = outcome['kind'], list(outcome.get('repeat_of') or []), list(outcome.get('revises') or [])\n        if kind == 'failed':\n            raise Refused(f\"comparison failed for {record['id']}: {outcome.get('reason', 'no reason given')}\")\n        if kind not in ('new', 'repeat', 'revision'):\n            raise Refused(f'unknown outcome {kind!r}')\n        if (kind == 'repeat') != bool(repeat_of) or len(repeat_of) > 1:\n            raise Refused(f\"a repeat names exactly one group; got {repeat_of} for outcome {kind}\")\n        if kind == 'revision' and not revises:\n            raise Refused('a revision names the group it revises')\n        for group_id in repeat_of + revises:\n            if group_id not in self.groups:\n                raise Refused(f'unknown group {group_id}')\n        target = repeat_of[0] if repeat_of else record['id']\n        if record['id'] in self.placement:\n            if self.placement[record['id']] != target:\n                raise Refused(f\"{record['id']} was placed in {self.placement[record['id']]}, not {target}\")\n            group = self.groups[target]\n            stored = next(r for r in [group['original']] + group['members'] if r['id'] == record['id'])\n            if {k: v for k, v in stored.items() if k != 'thesis_ids'} != {k: v for k, v in record.items() if k != 'thesis_ids'}:\n                raise Refused(f\"{record['id']} names a stored record with different content; a changed record needs a new id\")\n            self._link(group, record)\n            return target\n        if kind == 'repeat':\n            group = self.groups[target]\n            group['members'].append(copy.deepcopy(record))\n        else:\n            group = {'original': copy.deepcopy(record), 'members': [], 'links': {}, 'revises': []}\n            self.groups[target] = group\n            self.order.append(target)\n        self.placement[record['id']] = target\n        self._link(group, record)\n        for revised in revises:\n            if revised != target and not any(r['group'] == revised for r in group['revises']):\n                group['revises'].append({'group': revised, 'by': record['id']})\n        return target\n\n    def link_later(self, thesis_id, judge, before_article, batch=10):\n        \"\"\"Judge every group whose original arrived unlinked from an article before `before_article` against a newly opened thesis.\n        judge(group ids) returns {group id: True | False} or raises. Returns {'linked': [...], 'pending': [...], 'judged': n}.\"\"\"\n        self.opened_at.setdefault(thesis_id, before_article)\n        before_article = self.opened_at[thesis_id]\n        todo = [g for g in self.order if not self.groups[g]['original']['thesis_ids']\n                and self.groups[g]['original']['article'] < before_article and (thesis_id, g) not in self.judged]\n        linked, pending = [], []\n        for start in range(0, len(todo), batch):\n            ids = todo[start:start + batch]\n            answers = None\n            for _attempt in range(2):\n                try:\n                    answers = judge(ids)\n                    break\n                except Exception:   # tried twice, then reported as pending, never saved as a judgement\n                    answers = None\n            if answers is None:\n                pending += ids\n                continue\n            for group_id in ids:\n                self.judged[(thesis_id, group_id)] = bool(answers[group_id])\n                if answers[group_id]:\n                    self.groups[group_id]['links'].setdefault(thesis_id, self.groups[group_id]['original']['id'])\n                    linked.append(group_id)\n        if pending:\n            self.pending[thesis_id] = pending\n        else:\n            self.pending.pop(thesis_id, None)\n        return {'linked': linked, 'pending': pending, 'judged': len(todo) - len(pending)}\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _link(group, record):\n        for thesis_id in record['thesis_ids']:\n            group['links'].setdefault(thesis_id, record['id'])\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def articles(group):\n        \"\"\"Distinct source articles of a group, oldest first; two records from one article count once.\"\"\"\n        seen = []\n        for record in [group['original']] + group['members']:\n            if record['article'] not in seen:\n                seen.append(record['article'])\n        return seen\n\n    def dossier(self, thesis_id):\n        \"\"\"Group ids linked to a thesis, in creation order.\"\"\"\n        return [g for g in self.order if thesis_id in self.groups[g]['links']]\n\n\ndef labelled_passages(record):\n    \"\"\"Each passage as a reader sees it: the source text Step 1 found, labelled 'Quote', or, when Step 1 did not find it (verified\n    value None), the model's text labelled 'Unverified quote'. The model's own text stays in the record's `passages`. A record stored\n    before verification was carried shows its passages as 'Quote'.\"\"\"\n    verified = record.get('verified_passages') or record['passages']\n    return [('Quote', found) if found is not None else ('Unverified quote', passage) for passage, found in zip(record['passages'], verified)]\n\n\ndef record_text(record, label):\n    attribution = record['original_party'] or 'unknown party'\n    if record['reporting_speaker'] and record['reporting_speaker'] != record['original_party']:\n        attribution += f\", reported by {record['reporting_speaker']}\"\n    head = (f\"[{label}] {record['publication_date']} · {record['publisher'] or 'unknown publisher'} · {attribution} · tier {record['tier']}\"\n            f\" · stated {record['statement_date'] or 'unknown'} · period {record['evidence_period'] or 'unknown'}\")\n    quotes = '\\n'.join(f'  {label_of}: \"{p}\"' for label_of, p in labelled_passages(record))\n    return f\"{head}\\n  {record['summary']}\\n{quotes}\"\n\n\ndef group_text(library, group_id, label, labels, member_text=True, notes=()):\n    \"\"\"A group as a reader sees it: the original record, then each later report of the same statement in arrival order, with its own\n    text when `member_text` is set and as a source line otherwise. Distinct articles are counted; repeats are not called confirmation.\"\"\"\n    group = library.groups[group_id]\n    lines = [record_text(group['original'], label)]\n    if group['members']:\n        articles = library.articles(group)\n        publishers = {r['publisher'] for r in [group['original']] + group['members']}\n        lines.append(f'  Later reports of the same statement: {len(group[\"members\"])} records from {len(articles) - 1} further articles '\n                     f'({len(publishers)} publishers in all). Articles repeating a statement do not by themselves confirm it independently.')\n        for member in group['members']:\n            if member_text:\n                party = '' if member['original_party'] == group['original']['original_party'] else f\" · {member['original_party']}\"\n                quotes = ' '.join(f'\"{p}\"' if kind == 'Quote' else f'\"{p}\" (unverified)' for kind, p in labelled_passages(member))\n                lines.append(f\"    - {member['publication_date']} · {member['publisher']}{party}: {member['summary']}\\n      Quote: {quotes}\")\n            else:\n                lines.append(f\"    - {member['publication_date']} · {member['publisher']}\")\n    for revised in group['revises']:\n        lines.append(f\"  Revises [{labels[revised['group']]}].\" if revised['group'] in labels else '  Revises an entry outside this dossier.')\n    lines += [f'  {note}' for note in notes]\n    return '\\n'.join(lines)\n","numLines":166,"startLine":1,"totalLines":166}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HWTKjWvouUzJFbUTqWRGVF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
