1 prompt: c8, adopted (D387)\n557:### What the model receives\n563:### System prompt\n741:### Closing check\n764:### Proposed per-item input\n791:### Structured-output schema\n1082:### Illustrative output for the sample input (earlier Luna draft, kept as history)\n1151:### Mapping to the Step 1 diagram\n1163:### Request review and remaining limits\n1171:## 13. Step 2 prompt: Jev working draft\n1179:### What Jev receives\n1186:### Proposed comparison instruction\n1212:### Input to be inserted at runtime\n1227:## 14. Existing components to reference during the rebuild\n1231:### Thesis and evidence database\n1239:### Source pool and golden validation data\n1250:### Source data standing in for Hummingbird\n1258:### Existing extraction reference split\n1271:### Diagram-to-code map\n1293:## 15. Architecture challenge: questions before building\n1305:## 16. Future design: entity relationships and cross-entity linkage\n1309:### Why this is needed\n1313:### Separate, asynchronous relationship maintenance\n1323:### Illustration: a supplier disruption\n1327:### Questions to resolve before cross-entity production use\n1339:## 17. Implementation plan for review\n1345:### Working boundaries\n1353:### Milestone 0 — Prepare the first Step 1 run\n1365:### Milestone 1 — Make Step 1 runnable and inspectable\n1381:### Milestone 2 — Retrieve and compare prior evidence\n1392:### Milestone 3 — Save and read evidence and links\n1402:### Milestone 4 — Connect and review the four-step flow\n1412:### Decisions to resolve as the work reaches them\n1424:## 18. Luna draft and existing production compatibility review\n1428:### The concrete compatibility check\n1444:### What differs and why it matters\n1457:### Field ownership and proposed mapping\n1474:### Acceptance of the Step 1 handoff\n1478:### Prompt review and next design task\n1484:## 19. Claude review: verified findings and open choices"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78ccad56-ed8d-4e29-91b7-f576c6d2916d","uuid":"c7baafc6-2fe9-443d-bf8f-2fc78dc34a3a","timestamp":"2026-11-09T21:06:41.823Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"1:# Hivemind architecture: the hedge fund research brain\n5:## 1. What the system does\n15:## 2. Architecture at a glance\n54:## 3. The information the system works with\n68:## 4. Step 1: extract theses and evidence\n70:### Input\n76:### What the model decides\n87:### Output\n106:### Step 1 contract and the existing ledger\n118:### Example\n129:## 5. Step 2: find and compare related evidence\n131:### Why this is separate\n135:### Find candidate evidence\n143:### Compare with Jev\n178:## 6. Step 3: save evidence and links\n191:## 7. Step 4: judge the thesis\n201:## 8. Evaluate Step 1\n214:### Forward run and state review\n220:### Current Step 1 forward run\n226:### Prepared-source Step 1 replay\n236:### Citation-completion diagnostic\n242:### Page-time-order Step 1 replay\n248:### Step 1 source-faithfulness council\n256:### Proposed Step 1 link implementation\n270:### Step 1 link candidate: completed comparison\n278:### Trace: Kyber evidence omitted during extraction\n284:### Kyber trace: thesis-visibility diagnostic\n290:### Kyber trace: full article versus its source paragraph\n296:### Whole-article coverage council: prior attempts and next candidate\n302:### Whole-article coverage: completed order comparison\n310:### Completed review: 49 articles and 160 evidence items\n318:### Source handoff council: ongoing investigation\n376:### Source-fidelity council: what must be preserved\n384:### Step 1 joint review: causes and priorities\n404:### Execution 1: source text and event ordering\n427:### Execution 2–4: link, fidelity and topic review\n439:### July 8–9 Step 1 replay\n453:### Step 1 run replay\n459:### Exploratory playforward: H200 articles\n499:## 9. Walk one item through the system\n512:## 10. Open design questions\n523:## 11. Design boundary\n527:## 12. Step 1 prompt: c8, adopted (D387)\n557:### What the model receives\n563:### System prompt\n741:### Closing check\n764:### Proposed per-item input\n791:### Structured-output schema\n1082:### Illustrative output for the sample input (earlier Luna draft, kept as history)\n1151:### Mapping to the Step 1 diagram\n1163:### Request review and remaining limits\n1171:## 13. Step 2 prompt: Jev working draft\n1179:### What Jev receives\n1186:### Proposed comparison instruction\n1212:### Input to be inserted at runtime\n1227:## 14. Existing components to reference during the rebuild\n1231:### Thesis and evidence database\n1239:### Source pool and golden validation data\n1250:### Source data standing in for Hummingbird\n1258:### Existing extraction reference split\n1271:### Diagram-to-code map\n1293:## 15. Architecture challenge: questions before building\n1305:## 16. Future design: entity relationships and cross-entity linkage\n1309:### Why this is needed\n1313:### Separate, asynchronous relationship maintenance\n1323:### Illustration: a supplier disruption\n1327:### Questions to resolve before cross-entity production use\n1339:## 17. Implementation plan for review\n1345:### Working boundaries\n1353:### Milestone 0 — Prepare the first Step 1 run\n1365:### Milestone 1 — Make Step 1 runnable and inspectable\n1381:### Milestone 2 — Retrieve and compare prior evidence\n1392:### Milestone 3 — Save and read evidence and links\n1402:### Milestone 4 — Connect and review the four-step flow\n1412:### Decisions to resolve as the work reaches them\n1424:## 18. Luna draft and existing production compatibility review\n1428:### The concrete compatibility check\n1444:### What differs and why it matters\n1457:### Field ownership and proposed mapping\n1474:### Acceptance of the Step 1 handoff\n1478:### Prompt review and next design task\n1484:## 19. Claude review: verified findings and open choices","numLines":82,"totalLines":82},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01M9AyATcnTAmLu4wN8WTa6i","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mo